- CRYSTALLIZED: all five pips filled, and the whole bar frame overgrown at both ends with crooked grey-green salt crystals.
- CORRODED 3: the five pips replaced by three small round pale yellow-green bubbling lye drops.
ROW 2, head "STEEPED": three small square buff icons on dark stone faces, labels under them: "IN BRINE" (a small pool of murky teal water with foam rings under a pair of feet), "ON CRUST" (a patch of grey-green crooked salt crust under a pair of feet), "STEEPED" (a pale-gold upward chevron over a wave line, meaning more damage).
ROW 3, head "GROUND": two flat ground decals seen from the isometric camera, labels "BRINE POOL" and "SALT CRUST": an irregular murky teal puddle with foam edges and a strand of kelp; an irregular patch of grey-green gritty crust with a few crooked crystals.

